/target/
# A sweep writes its whole run under mutants.out/ — lock file, per-mutant logs
# and diffs, the outcome lists — and moves the previous run to mutants.out.old/
# beside it before it starts. Ignoring only the live directory is what let a
# `git add -A` commit a rotated sweep onto a branch.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/
.alder/
.claude/settings.local.json
